    "updated_at": "2022-03-25T17:26:00Z",
    "body": "Rather than open a new issue for this I will just add that I came here for a similar issue with go, where I have a shell script that creates a `go` alias to match the directory/project requirement, so that means when I run the `go`  command it reports the correct go version. \r\n\r\nBut the Starship prompt is (I think) using the `go version` command to display the version (which is often different to the project requirements). \r\n\r\nI'm not sure how to resolve this other than maybe having a hook that can refresh the prompt? I imagine if Starship is just calling out to the `go version` command, then hopefully the alias should be used instead at that point.\r\n\r\nNot the end of the world but just thought I'd raise it in case there's a way to work around this.",
